WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:10.639 align:start position:19%
Number two, cirming
fermented herring from Sweden. The

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:16.640 align:start position:19%
smelliest food on Earth. Scientifically,
they ferment the fish in cans for

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:21.600 align:start position:19%
months. The cans literally bulge from
the gas building up inside.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:28.080 align:start position:19%
One study measured it as one of the most
putrid food odors ever recorded.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:33.600 align:start position:19%
Science said so. Open one indoors and
the smell can clear a whole building.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:40.320 align:start position:19%
It's been banned on airplanes.
Banned on airplanes.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:46.719 align:start position:19%
Let that sink in. Your lunch is legally
a biohazard at 30,000 ft. Brave Swedes

00:00:44.559 --> 00:00:53.120 align:start position:19%
eat it outdoors with flatbread,
potatoes, and onions. Always in August,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.120 align:start position:19%
always upwind.

